  "summary": "Across 6 attacks x 2 datasets (455 K=3 panels each): score_manipulation (r=0.98), authority_bias (r=0.96), sycophancy (r=0.92), verbosity_bias (r=0.92) preserve K_eff ranking well. prompt_injection moderately disrupts (r=0.61, mean |dK|=0.25). position_bias heavily disrupts MI structure (r=0.08-0.60, mean |dK|=0.53-0.84), likely because position swapping uniformly decorrelates judges. Overall mean r=0.79. Conclusion: clean K_eff is a reliable proxy for 4/6 attacks; position_bias and prompt_injection require attacked-K_eff correction."
